    costRange:  '$50/hour &mdash; packages available. Call (316) 303-6195 to book.',
    intro:      'Diamond Springs Ranch offers riding lessons for beginners through intermediate riders, starting at $50/hour. Taught by people who ride these horses every day &mdash; not seasonal hires. Ages 5 and up. Whether it&rsquo;s your first time in a saddle or you&rsquo;re building on prior experience, the instruction at Diamond Springs Ranch is practical, patient, and grounded in real horsemanship.',
    body:       '<p>Riding lessons at Diamond Springs Ranch are taught by the same people who work with these horses every day on the ranch. That makes a difference &mdash; the instruction isn&rsquo;t scripted or manufactured for tourists. It&rsquo;s real horsemanship taught on horses the instructors know personally.</p><h2>Riding Lesson Pricing and Packages</h2><p>Lessons start at $50/hour. Package pricing is available for families and individuals who want to build a consistent lesson schedule. Call (316) 303-6195 to discuss lesson structure, package options, and scheduling. All riding lessons are by reservation.</p><h2>What Ages Can Take Riding Lessons at Diamond Springs Ranch?</h2><p>Riding lessons are open to all ages starting at 5 years old. Young children, teenagers, adults, and seniors all participate in lessons at the ranch. The instruction is matched to the student &mdash; complete beginners, riders who came off horses years ago and want to get back in the saddle, and intermediate riders looking to improve technique all find the right fit here.</p><h2>What Do Riding Lessons Cover?</h2><p>Beginner lessons cover the fundamentals: mounting and dismounting safely, basic seat position, steering, stopping, and basic trail pace. Intermediate lessons build on those foundations with more advanced riding skills. All lessons include a horsemanship component &mdash; understanding how to read a horse, how to approach and handle horses on the ground, and how to communicate with the animal. This is real equine education, not just a trail follow-the-leader experience.</p><h2>Book Riding Lessons Near Wichita</h2><p>Diamond Springs Ranch is 17 miles north of Wichita &mdash; a 25-minute drive from most Wichita neighborhoods, and even shorter from Newton. For families looking for riding lessons in the Wichita metro area, the ranch is the closest working-ranch option available.</p><p>Explore more experiences: <a href="/guided-horseback-rides/">Guided Trail Rides</a>, <a href="/horse-day-camp/">Horse Day Camp</a>, <a href="/highland-cattle-experience/">Highland Cattle Experience</a>. View our full <a href="/services/">ranch experience list</a>.</p>',
