    intro:      'Diamond Springs Ranch runs a Horse Day Camp every summer &mdash; June through August, ages 9 to 14, $250/week. It&rsquo;s a hands-on week of real horsemanship, animal care, and ranch life on a working Kansas ranch. Kids who come to camp leave knowing how to handle horses, not just ride them. One of the most popular summer programs for Wichita-area families.',
    body:       '<p>Horse Day Camp at Diamond Springs Ranch runs June through August and is built for kids ages 9 to 14 who want more than a trail ride. A week at camp includes daily hands-on horsemanship instruction, animal care and feeding, trail rides, Highland cattle encounters, and the kind of unstructured ranch time that kids raised in the suburbs rarely get.</p><h2>What Happens at Horse Day Camp?</h2><p>Each camp week covers riding basics and intermediate skills, ground handling, grooming and tack, horse health fundamentals, cattle observations, and ranch chores. Kids learn to work with horses as partners, not just passengers. The program is led by the Diamond Springs Ranch staff &mdash; the same people who work with these animals daily &mdash; so the instruction is grounded in real ranching rather than curated for optics.</p><h2>Camp Schedule and Pricing</h2><ul><li>Dates: June through August (specific weeks posted seasonally &mdash; call for current schedule)</li><li>Ages: 9&ndash;14</li><li>Price: $250/week</li><li>Book: <a href="https://fareharbor.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FareHarbor online booking</a> or call (316) 303-6195</li></ul><h2>Why Wichita Parents Choose Diamond Springs Ranch for Summer Horse Camp</h2><p>The alternatives for equine summer programs in the Wichita area are limited. Diamond Springs Ranch provides access to a working horse and cattle operation &mdash; not a riding school with a few horses in a suburban ring. Kids who complete camp week can handle, groom, tack, and ride a horse with confidence. At $250/week, it&rsquo;s one of the most accessible specialty summer programs in the region.</p><p>Explore more: <a href="/riding-lessons/">Riding Lessons</a>, <a href="/guided-horseback-rides/">Guided Trail Rides</a>, <a href="/highland-cattle-experience/">Highland Cattle Experience</a>. View all <a href="/services/">ranch experiences</a>.</p>',
